  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Expect on and off showers through Saturday. \nRainfall totals will be light Saturday, so the day wont be a \ncomplete washout.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1 DESCRIPTION...\nLow pressure remains positioned over the Prince Edward\nIsland/Nova Scotia region through Saturday, and we will remain\non the west side of the cyclonic circulation around this low\npressure, with some showers. Early this evening, showers are\nbeginning to dissipating a bit with the loss of daytime \nheating. However, late this evening into the overnight hours, a \nspoke of energy rotating west around the low pressure will bring\nanother wave of showers through the area. Nothing too crazy, \nbut some spots especially in the north could see an additional \nquarter inch of rain. A bit of a break in the showers toward \ndawn Saturday, then some more showers possible during the day \nSaturday, best chance being in the north with about a 30 percent\nchance of measurable rain at any one location. Not a washout \nday by any means, but you may need to dodge a shower. Quite \nbreezy Saturday with winds from the northeast gusting to around \n25 mph.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...Rain chances remain limited through midweek, \naccompanied by near to below normal temperatures. The next best \nchance for precipitation arrives Wednesday night into Thursday.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2 DESCRIPTION...\nNorth Atlantic blocking weakens Sunday evening allowing for the\nstacked low track NE. Expecting dry conditions between Sunday\ninto Tuesday with temperatures near or slightly below normal.\nHighs in the 70s with lows in the 40s but potentially some upper\n30s in the cold spots across Northern Maine on Monday AM. A weak\ncold front crosses the region Tuesday AM into Tuesday PM with\nisolated to scattered rain showers. Wednesday night into\nThursday much of the global ensembles are pointing to a more\nrobust 500mb shortwave in the northern stream to provide another\nchance of widespread rain showers. Significant uncertainty on\ntiming and how much rainfall we will end up with given the\ndifferences between showers and stratiform precip.",
